# Android local LLM — development proposal

{{ settings.warning }}

{{ settings.warning_es }}

This proposed app needs Android 13 or newer and an arm64 phone.
Its model import and memory use still need a physical phone check.
Use the START PDFs if this app will not install or load the model.

1. Open `android/OfflineLLM.apk` on the drive and install it.
   Do not follow a request to download a model or create an account.
2. Open the app's Settings and tap **Import GGUF Model**.
   Select `Model.gguf` from the drive. Wait for its local copy to finish.
   Stop if the phone has too little free storage.
3. Keep GPU Acceleration off for this proposed CPU setup.
4. Set **Context Size** to {{ settings.context_tokens }}.
   Set **Max Tokens** to {{ settings.max_output_tokens }}.
   Set the **Temperature** display to {{ settings.temperature }}.
   Set **CPU Threads** to {{ settings.threads }} only if the slider offers it.
5. Under **System Prompt**, choose **Custom**.
   Copy all of `system-en.txt` or `system-es.txt` from this companion into
   **Custom System Prompt**. Start a new chat after changing the prompt.
6. Read START for instructions before acting. These prompts use START section
   titles when full text does not fit; they do not replace the START PDFs.
7. Stop and start a new chat if the app reports a full context or a model error.
   Do not shorten a medical instruction to make it fit.

The app has optional read-aloud controls. Leave them off during the offline
check: they delegate to the phone's separately installed speech engine.

